{
  $schema: 'https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json',
  extends: [
    'config:best-practices',
    'group:linters',
    'group:allDigest',
  ],
  dependencyDashboard: {
    enabled: true,
    title: 'Dependency dashboard',
    labels: [
      'dependencies',
    ],
    header: '<p align="center">\n<picture>\n<source media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pureidlelabs/IncidentCompanion/main/assets/wordmark-dark.png">\n<img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pureidlelabs/IncidentCompanion/main/assets/wordmark-light.png" width="320" alt="IncidentCompanion">\n</picture>\n</p>\n\n<p align="center">\n<img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/cooldown-3%20days-6d97c4?style=flat-square&labelColor=1b2634" alt="cooldown: 3 days">\n<img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/vulnerabilities-no%20wait-3c5f8a?style=flat-square&labelColor=1b2634" alt="vulnerabilities: no wait">\n<img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/majors-on%20approval-e5ab5c?style=flat-square&labelColor=1b2634" alt="majors: on approval">\n<img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/gate-CI%20%2B%20merge%20queue-a87f57?style=flat-square&labelColor=1b2634" alt="gate: CI and merge queue">\n</p>\n\nTick a box under **Pending Approval** and the branch is raised; the migration is a session\'s work from there. Everything that is not a major merges itself: `gate` has to report green, and the merge queue rebuilds the branch against the `main` it is about to enter before it lands.',
    osvVulnerabilitySummary: 'all',
  },
  labels: [
    'dependencies',
  ],
  prHourlyLimit: 0,
  prConcurrentLimit: 5,
  major: {
    dependencyDashboardApproval: true,
  },
  osvVulnerabilityAlerts: true,
  vulnerabilityAlerts: {
    enabled: true,
    minimumReleaseAge: null,
    labels: [
      'dependencies',
      'security',
    ],
  },
  mise: {
    managerFilePatterns: [
      '/^\\.devcontainer/mise\\.toml$/',
    ],
  },
  customManagers: [
    {
      customType: 'regex',
      managerFilePatterns: [
        '/^\\.devcontainer/Dockerfile$/',
      ],
      matchStrings: [
        '# renovate: datasource=(?<datasource>\\S+) depName=(?<depName>\\S+)\\nARG \\w+=(?<currentValue>\\S+)',
      ],
    },
  ],
  lockFileMaintenance: {
    enabled: true,
    automerge: true,
  },
  packageRules: [
    {
      description: 'Anything that is not a major is a merge nobody would have read.',
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'minor',
        'patch',
        'pin',
        'pinDigest',
        'digest',
        'bump',
      ],
      automerge: true,
    },
    {
      description: 'The ORM and its kit share a release, and server/package.json pins the ORM a second time under overrides.',
      groupName: 'drizzle',
      matchPackageNames: [
        'drizzle-orm',
        'drizzle-kit',
      ],
    },
    {
      description: 'TypeScript 7',
      matchPackageNames: [
        'typescript',
      ],
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'major',
      ],
      prBodyNotes: [
        "**Blocked by `nest build`**, which drives the compiler through `createProgram`, `createIncrementalProgram`, `createWatchProgram` and `createEmitAndSemanticDiagnosticsBuilderProgram` (`@nestjs/cli/lib/compiler/`). TypeScript 7's own feature table lists `API` as *not ready*, so there is nothing for those calls to reach; check `tsc/README.md` at the tag rather than the release notes.",
        'Separately: `@thallesp/nestjs-better-auth` peers on `typescript` `^5.9.2 || ^6.0.0`. `.npmrc` sets `legacy-peer-deps=true`, so the install will succeed and say nothing -- check `npm ls typescript` for one deduped copy rather than reading that silence as agreement.',
      ],
    },
    {
      description: 'react-aria-components 1.22',
      matchPackageNames: [
        'react-aria-components',
      ],
      dependencyDashboardApproval: true,
      prBodyNotes: [
        "**Blocked by `react-aria@3.53`'s `useExitAnimation`**, which waits on `Promise.all(...).catch(() => {})` where 3.52 used `Promise.allSettled`. An overlay closed while its Motion entry animation is still running sees that animation cancelled, the rejection is swallowed, and the overlay never unmounts: an invisible modal stays over the page. 3.53.1 still has it. Tick once `react-aria/dist/private/utils/animation.mjs` at the new version settles a cancelled animation, and run the story tier: the cheat sheet's `Raised over the case` is the story that catches it.",
      ],
    },
    {
      description: 'OpenSpec 1.14.1 and later',
      matchPackageNames: [
        '@fission-ai/openspec',
      ],
      dependencyDashboardApproval: true,
      prBodyNotes: [
        '**Blocked by a new validator rule**: requirement text over 500 characters is a warning, `--strict` turns it into a failure, and the limit is a constant (`MAX_REQUIREMENT_TEXT_LENGTH`) with no setting. 117 requirements across 20 specs exceed it. Ticking this is deciding to rewrite those requirements, which is a change under `openspec/changes/`, not a dependency bump.',
      ],
    },
    {
      description: 'The framework moves as one, across the repositories it is published from.',
      groupName: 'nest',
      matchPackageNames: [
        '@nestjs/**',
      ],
    },
    {
      description: 'The images built from this tree do not exist in any registry.',
      matchDatasources: [
        'docker',
      ],
      matchPackageNames: [
        '/^incidentcompanion-/',
      ],
      enabled: false,
    },
    {
      description: 'The release-age floor covers every ecosystem, not only npm.',
      matchDatasources: [
        'docker',
        'github-actions',
        'pypi',
      ],
      minimumReleaseAge: '3 days',
      internalChecksFilter: 'strict',
    },
    {
      description: 'Update types whose age Renovate cannot establish.',
      matchDatasources: [
        'docker',
        'github-actions',
        'pypi',
      ],
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'lockFileMaintenance',
        'pin',
        'pinDigest',
        'replacement',
      ],
      minimumReleaseAge: null,
    },
    {
      description: 'The services a run needs are named twice and move as one.',
      groupName: 'stack services',
      matchDatasources: [
        'docker',
      ],
      matchPackageNames: [
        'postgres',
        'redis',
      ],
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'major',
        'minor',
        'patch',
      ],
    },
  ],
}
